  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "Evidence: All three completed experiments share scvi_n200 + resnet50 + multiprofile, and clearly show transformer aggregation (0.713) > avgpool (0.678) and weighted fusion (0.713) > concat (0.688). The best config (config_004, 0.713 acc) still uses a relatively modest RNA encoder (scvi_n200, a VAE) and a standard image encoder (resnet50). The largest remaining uncertainty is whether upgrading the RNA encoder to scgpt—a pretrained single-cell foundation model that captures richer biological semantics—will yield a meaningful accuracy gain while keeping the proven transformer+weighted architecture. This experiment (config_028: scgpt, resnet50, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) isolates the RNA-encoder variable as a direct, minimal extension of the current best. It is the best use of experiment 4 because it tests the single most impactful unexplored axis (RNA representation quality) before committing to the more expensive joint upgrade (scgpt + ViT-L). Expected relative cost: moderate-to-high, roughly 7–8 GPU hours (scgpt is larger than scvi_n200 but resnet50 and transformer aggregation keep it below the ViT-L variants), which is acceptable given 6 experiments remain and the potential accuracy uplift justifies the spend."
}

